{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head d4a1def7179e9a243228625d2cefd7af92d50bbd, and I accept the two commits after the gate with no new gate. No deployed Worker or desktop AI app ran this code, as your note states.\n\n**The change.** `#readExact` now strips `text` from the result and keeps the facts: commits, truncation and paths. The display holds the text, and the result's own text says \"Diff shown on the page.\" My search of `packages/mcp/browser/main.ts` and `apps/views/src` finds nothing that reads the result's `text`, which matches your note. `copyOf` keeps the fallback for an ordinary card on a host that drops `structuredContent`, because `bridge.ts:94-97` parses that text, and over 32 KiB it says where the result is. The new test measures the point of the request: one copy of the text, under 44 KiB at about 40 KiB of text, and the display still holds the whole body. Your three controls each restore a copy and turn it red.\n\n**A side benefit.** The model's text channel now carries less of a repository's content on a large read, because a read's result no longer repeats that text, and over 32 KiB the frame's text no longer does either. Under 32 KiB, the frame's text still holds the display with its body. So this does not remove repository text from what a host can pass on. The J2 acceptance should watch what the app gives its model.\n\n**The limit: a person would meet it as a plain failure.** On a host that drops `structuredContent`, a read over about 32 KiB of JSON gives \"The app tool returned no readable card data\", and its credential is spent. MCP Apps passes `structuredContent`, so I accept this. The J2 acceptance's report on the desktop app decides whether it matters.\n\n**The commits after the gate: accepted.**\n- 0a120cee and 42c33abf have the same tree, cc91608b, so the gate applies. Only the trailer changed, and the `Promise` trailer now reads in full.\n- The merge of main dea4a192 shares one file with this head, `view-sessions.test.ts`, on other lines. Main's other files do not meet these two source files, and no gate is owed for that shared test file. I reran it with `view-resources.test.ts` (16 passed), `change-view.scope.test.ts` (17 passed) and `security-entry-points` (10 pass) on the merged tree.\n\n**Your next-edit item.** You are right that this head does not touch it. It stays yours.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is 8adb8fd9…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 42c33abf, exit 0, with 3533 and 1013 tests. check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (1001, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (3, 0 flagged) pass. The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the controls.\n\n**Architecture.** The result states facts and the display holds the text, which gives each its own job. No hosted route changes.\n\n**Security.** No authority changes. A credential is still spent once for each read, and no credential enters a frame.\n\n**Simplification.** This removes five of six copies. Nothing more to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:05a8eb9aa102dcd67abfc0c5e7e267e5bfb77a20","binding":"assigned","head":"d4a1def7179e9a243228625d2cefd7af92d50bbd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d669a0e2d2f6f61f21e8b17df32f0b5a94491f21\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e93f86a8de35b86afbbdc7bab52d29a8e9fe3ecc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d669a0e2d2f6f61f21e8b17df32f0b5a94491f21","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}